# XCU vi
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests type keystrokes at a private pseudo-terminal (core/pcpty.c) and read
# back the edited file. What the screen shows is not observed.

assertion  XCU.vi.001
anchor     utilities/vi.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/vi.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/vi.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      untestable
since      1992
says       vi shows the buffer on the screen, and the -r, -t and -w options and
           the remaining visual-mode commands (scrolling, marks, buffers,
           searches, shell filters) behave as the page defines.
reason     The screen contents depend on the terminal type and are not defined
           in a form a script can compare; recovery and tag files need state
           the page leaves to the implementation. Only the editing commands
           whose effect on the file is exact are tested.

assertion  XCU.vi.002
anchor     utilities/vi.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       Writing the unchanged buffer with :wq leaves the file as it was and vi
           exits zero.
test       t/002-write-quit.sh

assertion  XCU.vi.003
anchor     utilities/vi.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       UP
